          "python",
          "# Document data sources and potential biases\nDATA_DOCUMENTATION = \"\"\"\nDataset: Credit Approval Records (2020-2024)\n\nSource: Bank transaction data\n- Collected from 5 major U.S. banks\n- Represents ~1M customers\n\nDemographics:\n- Age: 18-75, mean=42\n- Income: $20k-$500k, median=$75k\n- Gender: 45% Female, 55% Male (self-reported, optional)\n- Race/Ethnicity: NOT collected (privacy-preserving choice)\n\nKnown Biases:\n- Underrepresented: customers <25 and >65\n- Income skew: higher-income customers (median >general population)\n- Geographic: urban-biased (80% urban, 20% rural)\n\nExclusions:\n- Customers with previous fraud: removed\n- Incomplete applications: removed\n- Reason: these groups are underrepresented\n\nLimitations:\n- Model should not be used for customers outside collected demographics\n- Higher uncertainty for rural customers\n- Performance may degrade for non-English speakers\n\"\"\"\n\n# Implement consent and opt-out\ndef apply_data_consent(dataframe, user_preferences):\n    \"\"\"Respect user preferences: opt-out, deletion rights.\"\"\"\n    \n    # Users who opted out\n    opted_out = dataframe[dataframe['user_id'].isin(\n        user_preferences[user_preferences['consent'] == False]['user_id']\n    )]\n    \n    # Delete or anonymize\n    dataframe = dataframe[~dataframe.index.isin(opted_out.index)]\n    \n    # Right to deletion: remove historical records\n    for user_id in user_preferences[user_preferences['delete_request'] == True]['user_id']:\n        dataframe = dataframe[dataframe['user_id'] != user_id]\n    \n    return dataframe"
        ]
